
` THE CURSOR COMES AND GOES. the cursor is not there while a board comes in, and it is not there in info
` mode, where it would look like something that can be picked. see fish_routines_cursorshow.
`
` WHEN A BOARD COMES IN, the cursor waits until the last fish is in, and then it pops in: it swells up
` from nothing, a little past its size and back, with a puff of bubbles. the entrance of a game, and the
` little boards of the tutorial, ask for it with cursorArrive(). a move that starts in the middle of it
` ends it at once, so that the cursor is never in the way of a move.
global CURSOR_ARRIVE_ON = 0 `1 from cursorArrive() until the cursor is all the way in
global CURSOR_ARRIVE_AT = 0 `the game ms() that it starts to pop in
global CURSOR_ARRIVE_POPPED = 0 `1 once it has started, and the bubbles have gone up
global CURSOR_ARRIVE_MS = 320 `how long it takes to pop in
global CURSOR_ARRIVE_BUBBLES = 7 `how many bubbles come off it

` IN INFO MODE, the cursor fades away while the panel comes in, and back while it goes. info_open and
` info_close say which way, with CURSOR_INFO_HIDE, and cursorShowStep() takes it there.
global CURSOR_INFO_HIDE = 0 `1 while info mode is open, or opening
global CURSOR_INFO_SHOW# = 1.0 `how much of the cursor shows, from 0 to 1
global CURSOR_INFO_FADE_MS# = 150 `how long it takes to fade all the way, the same as the panel
global CURSOR_SHOW_LAST_MS = 0
global CURSOR_SHOW_DIRTY = 0 `1 while the cursor is not as it always is, so that it is put back once, when it is
